    {
      "chose": "Cause: `layoutFrame` laid each why (and the note on your pick) under its card and only checked that it stayed above the frame's foot, never whether it met the card under it, so with cards stacked in a column the whys sat over the next card's words. Now a try whose whys or note meet another card or another why is passed over, like one that runs past the foot (the old last try, verdicts only under the cards whatever the room, included); then come \"longin\" (verdicts only, in each card's corner under its words) and last \"none\". Where nothing meets a card the tries and their order are as before, so cards in a row lay out as they did (the row still folds behind \"…\" at 1024 × 660)",
      "id": "a34",
